{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Why do you cry to Me?</b> For he was indeed included in \"the children of Israel cried out to YHWH\" (Exodus 14:10). However, Moses' cry was not out of fear of Pharaoh and his army, for he had already declared to Israel the fall and death of the Egyptians, as he said: \"you will never see them again forever; YHWH will fight for you\" (Exodus 14:13–14). Rather, his cry was because of the princes of Israel who brazenly spoke, saying \"Is it because there are no graves?\" (Exodus 14:11), and he supposed that for this reason they would not heed him to enter into the sea. Therefore He said to him: why do you cry to Me about this — for you indeed suspect competent men." "<b>Speak to the children of Israel and let them journey.</b> And they will not defy your word."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "Reading בכשרים as 'capable/competent men,' i.e., Israel's leaders whom Moses wrongly suspects of being beyond persuasion. The meaning is somewhat compressed in the original."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:29.801895125Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}